      "updated": 1761020406714,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Virtual Waiting Queue\nfor Extremely Popular\nEvents",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Virtual Waiting Queue\nfor Extremely Popular\nEvents",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3i1ETkA8Dq3sMfDGXisNu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 24676.984539939996,
      "y": 3089.9821568215007,
      "width": 510.3992919921875,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "KJ4uPU_pXIvV6fDnk-qJ3"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bfV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1293895846,
      "version": 985,
      "versionNonce": 328039846,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1761020900882,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Admin enabled virtual waiting \n  queue system to manage user access\n\n1. When user requests to view booking page,\nthey are placed in virtual queue. we will\nestablish a websocket connection with their\nclient and add user to the queue using unique\nwebsocket connection.\n2. Based on certain criteria (ex: tickets booked),\n   dequeue user from front of the queue. Notify\n   the user via websocket connection that they can\n   proceed to purchase tickets.\n3. At the same time update DB to reflect that this user is\nallowed to access purchase page.\n    ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Admin enabled virtual waiting \n  queue system to manage user access\n\n1. When user requests to view booking page,\nthey are placed in virtual queue. we will\nestablish a websocket connection with their\nclient and add user to the queue using unique\nwebsocket connection.\n2. Based on certain criteria (ex: tickets booked),\n   dequeue user from front of the queue. Notify\n   the user via websocket connection that they can\n   proceed to purchase tickets.\n3. At the same time update DB to reflect that this user is\nallowed to access purchase page.\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
