      "updated": 1761645081300,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5.1 Handling 1M req/sec, How ??",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5.1 Handling 1M req/sec, How ??",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3nws4zMhif035v2zpF8Xo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 35149.08875191949,
      "y": 788.8770038275532,
      "width": 827.1988525390625,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bs1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 587222095,
      "version": 621,
      "versionNonce": 405901967,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1761645427123,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- A typical Redis instance can handle 100,000 - 200,000 operations/second\n- Since each request performs HMGET and HSET, it falls back to 50,000-100,000.\n- So we think, multiple instances should do it, but it is way complex\n    - Partitioning the data so each request knows which redis instance to talk to\n\n\n- Consisting Hashing should be used\n    1. For Authenticated users : Hash User ID to determine which Redis shared stores the data.\n    2. For Public APIs : hash IP address\n    3. For APIKey requests : Hash API Key.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- A typical Redis instance can handle 100,000 - 200,000 operations/second\n- Since each request performs HMGET and HSET, it falls back to 50,000-100,000.\n- So we think, multiple instances should do it, but it is way complex\n    - Partitioning the data so each request knows which redis instance to talk to\n\n\n- Consisting Hashing should be used\n    1. For Authenticated users : Hash User ID to determine which Redis shared stores the data.\n    2. For Public APIs : hash IP address\n    3. For APIKey requests : Hash API Key.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
