      "updated": 1761661533811,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Problem is this: what if new jobs created are expected to run in < 5m, we would either miss it or wait for next 5 mins for cron to pick up\n- Or we could try to put directly on to the message queue (kafka), but it always appends to the queue, if queue already have 5 minute window of jobs??",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Problem is this: what if new jobs created are expected to run in < 5m, we would either miss it or wait for next 5 mins for cron to pick up\n- Or we could try to put directly on to the message queue (kafka), but it always appends to the queue, if queue already have 5 minute window of jobs??",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
