      "text": "5.4 Allow searching by predefined location names such as cities or neighborhoods",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5.4 Allow searching by predefined location names such as cities or neighborhoods",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rDsTc-eH2-JyMn7Ch6EbY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 136827.36038046755,
      "y": 99.88227299806726,
      "width": 935,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0xZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1244645168,
      "version": 245,
      "versionNonce": 788303312,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763101744060,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Go from location name to polygon (List of points and come from variety of sources)\n    Ex: GeoJSON\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Feature\",\n          \"geometry\": {\n            \"type\": \"Point\",\n            \"coordinates\": [125.6, 10.1]\n          },\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"name\": \"Silicon Valley\"\n          }\n        }\n    \n2. Use that polygon to filter a set of businesses that exist within it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Go from location name to polygon (List of points and come from variety of sources)\n    Ex: GeoJSON\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Feature\",\n          \"geometry\": {\n            \"type\": \"Point\",\n            \"coordinates\": [125.6, 10.1]\n          },\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"name\": \"Silicon Valley\"\n          }\n        }\n    \n2. Use that polygon to filter a set of businesses that exist within it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
